Provenance & retained upstream notice
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

self.code-eval is a fully vendored, renamed fork of the BigCode Evaluation
Harness (https://github.com/bigcode-project/bigcode-evaluation-harness),
originally licensed Apache-2.0. It was previously carried as self.bigcode-eval;
the Python package was renamed bigcode_eval -> code_eval.

The fork point is pinned in our history at upstream commit
`8fc5bae6479c4fbbb28c3f8b644f6a15b3f3b5bd` ("Update multiple.py", 2025-07-15),
the last BigCode Evaluation Harness commit before self.ai-specific work began
(`f0a5a97`, "built an api to wrap the testing harness"). No upstream release
tag exists at that point; the commit hash is the precise reference. The full
upstream git history up to that commit is preserved verbatim in this repo's
history — nothing was squashed.

Why fully vendored: self.ai licenses the combined work under GPLv3. Apache-2.0
is one-way compatible with GPLv3, so the upstream code is included here under
GPLv3 while its original Apache-2.0 license text and attribution are retained in
LICENSE.bigcode-apache-2.0. A GPLv3 combined work cannot be contributed back to
an Apache-2.0 upstream, so self.code-eval is a hard vendor: we do not track or
push to the original project. self.code-eval is not affiliated with, endorsed
by, or connected to the BigCode project.

self.code-eval is the catch-all harness for code-focused evaluation tasks;
more specific code-eval harnesses are forked from it.

The original Apache-2.0 license text is preserved verbatim in
LICENSE.bigcode-apache-2.0.
